    "sourceValidation": {
      "sourceLifeCall": "Projectile.OnTick @0x18091882d; MethodSpec 291686 through usage slot 0x188aef0b0 is BattleUtil.ValidAndAlive for the saved source ObjectPtr.",
      "observations": [
        "LinkProjectile returns true from get_stopWhenSourceInvalid on the stock branch. Harpoon, Laser and Lasso inherit it.",
        "Harpoon samples absent source as base force zero in this arithmetic branch, then independently checks validity of the saved target and source before the first BeginPull.",
        "NetCatcher initializes source force bonus to zero at 0x18091fb04 and skips the getter when the source Unity object is absent.",
        "A zero fallback in the force calculation does not establish an actual attack that continues after source loss."
      ]
    },
    "firstTouch": {
      "zeroBaseForce": "Harpoon @0x18091e81a and NetCatcher @0x18091fc48 can exit before BeginPull.",
      "arrivalStop": "Harpoon @0x18091e56d and NetCatcher @0x18091f964 branch to stop/cleanup before virtual BeginPull on first touch if configured to end on reach.",
      "arrivalHold": "The alternative zeroes the force argument and may register via BeginPull. The preceding TryEarlyStopPull only zeroes velocity when this same source is already the sole effective source.",
      "beginSlot": 234,
      "endSlot": 235
    },
    "positionAndEnd": [
      "The selected manual physics path simulates at 0x18065b2a2, commits Unbalance position at 0x18065b3ab, and runs CoroutineSimulator at 0x18065b48c.",
      "The continuation reads committed positions. A stop can also originate in the earlier ordinary projectile update.",
      "Where attachment/target/type guards permit, Harpoon and NetCatcher stop invoke the target EndPull slot before SearchBlockeeImmediate on a valid Character source.",
      "EndPull can synchronously tick the unbalance state after source removal; its OnEndPulling callback is later in the method and requires the relevant projectile source. Re-search is conditional and can reject a still-unbalanced target."
    ],
